🔵 14. Terraform Best Practices
🧠 Why Best Practices Matter

👉 Terraform can become difficult to manage if code is not structured properly

Best practices help you build:

Clean code
Reusable modules
Safer deployments
Team-friendly workflows

🔥 Important Best Practices
1. Use Modules

👉 Split infrastructure into logical reusable modules

Examples:

VPC
EKS
RDS
Load balancer

2. Avoid Hardcoding

👉 Use variables instead of fixed values

Examples:

region
instance type
CIDRs
environment names

3. Use Remote State

👉 Store state in S3 and use DynamoDB locking

Why?

Team collaboration
State safety
Conflict prevention

4. Do Not Commit State Files

👉 Never commit:

`terraform.tfstate`
`terraform.tfstate.backup`

5. Use Clear Naming

👉 Use meaningful names for resources, variables, and modules

6. Add Common Tags

👉 Tag resources with:

Environment
Project
Owner
ManagedBy

7. Use `terraform fmt` and `validate`

👉 Always format and validate before apply

8. Protect Production Changes

👉 Review `terraform plan` carefully before running `apply`

9. Keep Secrets Secure

👉 Do not hardcode passwords, keys, or tokens

Use:

secret managers
CI/CD secrets
sensitive variables

10. Keep Environments Separate

👉 Use workspaces or separate tfvars/environment folders when needed

11. Prefer `for_each` When Keys Matter

👉 Helps keep resource identity stable

12. Use Provisioners Only When Necessary

👉 Prefer user data, cloud-init, Helm, or config management tools

🔥 Team Best Practices

Use Git for version control
Use pull requests for review
Use CI/CD for plan and apply
Use remote state
Use code review before production changes

🧠 Interview Questions
❓ What are Terraform best practices?

👉
"Important Terraform best practices include using modules, remote state, variables, proper tagging, secure secret handling, and validating plans before apply."

❓ Why should you avoid hardcoding?

👉 Because it reduces reusability and makes environment management difficult

✅ Quick Summary
Terraform best practices help make infrastructure safer, cleaner, and easier to maintain in team environments
